 ## Background
-Originated in the context of data-distributed parallel ray-traced volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. It was developed as an alternative to fixed viewpoint partitioning to handle changing viewpoints in animation sequences [S1, unofficial]. The method is similar to front-to-back traversals of BSP-trees and octrees [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Developed for data-distributed parallel ray-traced volume rendering [S1][S2, S3, unofficial]. It serves as an alternative to fixed viewpoint partitioning to handle changing viewpoints in animation sequences [S2, S3, unofficial]. The traversal logic is similar to well-known front-to-back traversals of BSP-trees and octrees [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
